Review the supplied requirement and code as written. Return either NO_FINDING or one or more findings in the exact requested format. Do not use tools. Do not exceed 120 words.

Apply the agent-first Clean Code review contract: trace behavior against the requirement, check boundary and failure paths, distinguish evidence from assumption, report only actionable defects, and preserve correct silence when no defect is proven. Stop after the bounded review pass.

Requirement:
Authenticated webhook events have immutable unique IDs. Apply each event's database effects exactly once under concurrent delivery; a failed application must remain retryable. All effects in applyAccountChange use the supplied transaction.

Code:
export async function applyEvent(event: AccountEvent): Promise<void> {
  await db.transaction(async (tx) => {
    const claimed = await tx.query(
      `INSERT INTO processed_events (event_id)
       VALUES ($1)
       ON CONFLICT (event_id) DO NOTHING
       RETURNING event_id`,
      [event.id],
    );

    if (claimed.rowCount === 0) {
      return;
    }

    await applyAccountChange(tx, event);
  });
}


Response format:
Return exactly NO_FINDING if there is no actionable correctness defect. Otherwise return one line exactly as FINDING|<severity>|<line>|<description>, where severity is HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW, line is one positive integer, and description contains no pipe or newline. Report at most one finding.
